---
import Ide from "./_Ide.astro";
import Page from "./_Page.astro";
import { PY_AREA, TERM_DONE, TERM_INPUT } from "./_samples";

export const prerender = false;
---

<Page
  title="Mobile"
  lead="The stacked layout on a 360px-wide screen, as settled by the committee. Resize the window to see the real responsive behaviour; the phone frame is fixed at 360px."
>
  <section class="mt-8">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Stacked, with a pinned input field</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      Editor above, terminal below, both capped in height; same component as on desktop, no mode to switch. When the
      program waits for input, a one-line field pinned under the terminal takes the typing, so the on-screen keyboard
      never hides the cursor. The toolbar wraps: hint text hides, buttons stay.
    </p>
    <div class="mockup-phone mx-auto">
      <div class="mockup-phone-camera"></div>
      <div class="mockup-phone-display w-[360px] overflow-y-auto bg-base-100 px-3 pb-3 pt-10 text-base-content">
        <p class="font-display text-sm font-semibold">3. Rectangle area</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs">Write <code class="font-mono">area(width, height)</code> and read both values from the user.</p>
        <Ide class="mt-3" mode="answer" language="python" code={PY_AREA} state="waiting-input" terminal={TERM_INPUT} savedAt="14:32" compact inputBar />
        <p class="mb-1 mt-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">After the run</p>
        <Ide mode="answer" language="python" code={PY_AREA} state="done" terminal={TERM_DONE} lastRun="0.3 s" savedAt="14:32" compact />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-200/30 p-4 text-sm">
    <p class="font-semibold">Discarded: Code / Terminal tabs</p>
    <p class="mt-1">
      One pane at a time with a tab strip was the alternative. The committee picked the stacked layout (round 6, U1):
      no state to switch, output always next to the code, and the pinned input field solves the keyboard problem in
      either layout.
    </p>
  </section>
</Page>
